Z||000029||BellaFiero||07-05-2000||11:43 AM||||Big time into the raverific music. Alot of Rabbit... love trance and surreal tech. Gotta love the eighties music. I have a Jensen 10" subwoofer in a double ported box sitting in the passenger floorboard ( my Crystal has to put her feet on either side of the damned thing  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ) and I like songs with a lot of bass. Everything's amplified and it sounds incredibly clear, loud, and it'll change your heart beat when the bass hits  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. I love pulling up next to the big boats that are belting our Notorious B.I.G. and just letting loose with a little Juvenile or with some Eifel 65. People wonder how a car so small could be so loud. I love riding with my girl... there is nothing better than the windows half-down on a fall day, out cruising with a beautiful blonde in your freshly-waxed sports car, slamming out some fine music. I love Creedence Clearwater, Duran Duran, Eurythmics, Garbage, London After Midnight, KMFDM, Rabbit in the Moon, the Bar-Kays, Beastie Boys, Rage against the Machine, Metallica, Megadeath, Lords of Acid, Stone Temple, Creed, Van Bran 3000, Chris Isaac, Rod Stewart, the Stones, The Clash, and definitely, without a doubt, the Cars.||||reg||6
